course: dictionary
lesson: 10570
title: The prefix un- and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word uncooked is made of two parts. Un- means not, and cooked means heated until it is ready to eat. Put them together and uncooked means not cooked, which is also called raw. Once you know un- means not, you can work out other words too, like unhappy, unkind and untidy.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs, so they are eaten only when properly cooked.» The sentence tells you that uncooked meat can make you ill, so it must mean meat that has not been cooked yet. Try the swap: "raw meat can carry germs" still makes sense, so raw is a good match.
explain: Uncooked does not always mean unsafe. Some uncooked food, such as fruit and salad, is fine to eat. The context tells you which food the writer means, so read the whole sentence before you decide what the word means.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so uncooked means not cooked.
fact: «Uncooked» means not cooked; raw. You can say uncooked rice, uncooked chicken or uncooked dough.
fact: Uncooked meat, eggs and flour can carry germs, so they must be cooked properly before eating.
fact: Some uncooked foods, like fruit and salad, are fine to eat without cooking.
fact: Uncooked rice grows bigger when it is cooked.
exercise: «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs.» What does uncooked mean? | Fully finished | Covered in sauce | *Not cooked | Very cold
exercise: What does the un- in uncooked mean? | *Not | Before | Very | Again
exercise: Which of these foods is fine to eat without cooking? | Uncooked dough | Raw chicken | Uncooked eggs | *Fresh salad
test: Mum says, "The rice is still uncooked." What does she mean? | It is too hot to touch | *It has not been cooked yet | It has been cooked twice | It came in a packet
test: «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs.» According to the sentence, what can uncooked meat carry? | *Germs | Rice | Sunshine | Happiness
exam: Which word means the same as uncooked? | Frozen | Hot | *Raw | Cooked
